1.What are some common hyperparameters of decision tree models, and how do they affect the model's performance?
max_depth:
=>Defines the maximum depth of the tree.
=>A larger depth increases model complexity and may cause overfitting.
=>A smaller depth creates a simpler model and may lead to underfitting.

min_samples_split:
=>Minimum number of samples required to split a node.
=>Higher values reduce unnecessary splits and help avoid overfitting.

min_samples_leaf:
=>Minimum number of samples required in a leaf node.
=>Larger values produce smoother and more generalized predictions.

max_leaf_nodes:
=>Limits the number of leaf nodes in the tree.
=>Helps control tree size and reduces complexity.

criterion:
=>Measures the quality of a split.
=>Common options: gini and entropy.
=>Different criteria may slightly affect accuracy and split selection.

splitter:
=>Determines how splits are chosen.
=>best selects the best split, while random selects random splits.

max_features:
=>Number of features considered for splitting at each node.
=>Lower values reduce overfitting and improve randomness.

class_weight:
=>Assigns weights to classes.
=>Useful for handling imbalanced datasets.

ccp_alpha:
=>Used for pruning the tree.
=>Higher values remove more branches and reduce overfitting.

random_state:
=>Controls randomness in the model.
=>Ensures reproducible results.

Effect on Model Performance:
=>Increasing tree complexity improves training accuracy but may cause overfitting.
=>Reducing complexity improves generalization but may lead to underfitting.
=>Proper hyperparameter tuning helps achieve better accuracy and stability.


2. What is the difference between the Label encoding and One-hot encoding?
Label Encoding:
=>In Label Encoding, each category is assigned a unique numerical value.
=>It uses only one column to represent categories.
=>It is suitable for ordinal data where order is important.
=>It may create an unwanted ranking between categories.

One-Hot Encoding:
=>In One-Hot Encoding, separate binary columns are created for each category.
=>Each category is represented using 0 and 1 values.
=>It is suitable for nominal data where no order exists.
=>It avoids the problem of assigning ranking to categories.
